  "reasoning": "For 2026, Mississippi\u2019s key federal race is the U.S. Senate contest between Republican incumbent Cindy Hyde-Smith and Democrat Scott Colom, with all four House incumbents also on the ballot.[10][12][15] Recent coverage and fundraising reports describe Hyde-Smith as a clear favorite in a state that has not elected a Democrat to the Senate since 1982, despite Colom\u2019s unusually strong fundraising and increased national attention to the race.[8][10][15] Mississippi\u2019s statewide Cook PVI is around R+11, and current expert and media characterizations frame the Senate race as still leaning Republican by mid-single digits rather than a true toss-up, so I estimate a roughly 6-point Republican edge at this stage.[1][9][10]",
